.TH AVR\-ARTIFACT\-GET 1 "" "avr 0.5.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-artifact-get \- Get metadata for ART_ID in the selected repository.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr artifact get
[OPTIONS] ART_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Get metadata for ART_ID in the selected repository.
.PP
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIARTIFACT_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug; defaults to the configured organization.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository name or ID; defaults to the current git repository.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-artifact (1),
.BR avr-artifact-delete (1),
.BR avr-artifact-download (1),
.BR avr-artifact-list (1)
